      "content": "Taking even a reduced dose of Adderall poses serious risks because stimulants combine with hyperthyroidism to dangerously increase your heart rate, blood pressure, and body temperature. Since you mentioned feeling \"wired\" and having a fast heart rate already, reducing the dose is likely insufficient to manage those symptoms and could still lead to a cardiac event. Please contact your doctor, urgent care, or a poison control center immediately rather than attempting to self-adjust your medication today.",
